 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-23",
  "asof": "2026-09-25 09:59 UTC",
  "headline": "Okta built a consortium and Alphabet raised its bill \u2014 the AI trade split into two in a single session",
  "standfirst": "Okta used its investor day to launch the Blueprint Alliance with AWS, CrowdStrike, Google Cloud, Salesforce, ServiceNow, Zscaler and Wiz, and made Okta for AI Agents generally available at a 25-37.5% pricing uplift; the stock rose 4.46% to 205.38, above +1R. Alphabet went the other way, down 3.58% to 334.98, after raising 2026 capex guidance to $195-205bn in the same week OpenAI cut GPT-6 API prices by roughly half and Anthropic shipped Opus 5.5 about 40% cheaper. Underneath both, the ten-year set a 52-week high at 5.106% and the five-year cleared 5% for the first time since 2007 \u2014 not on oil or inflation but on a PMI at a five-year high, which took the Russell down 1.60% and the Nasdaq 1.11%. GOOG went from +1.07R to +0.45R. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged.",
